course: dictionary
lesson: 5907
title: Marigold: a flower with more than one kind
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A marigold is a garden plant with bright orange or yellow flowers. You can work out what a word means from the words around it. «Families decorate graves with orange marigolds and make sugar skulls.» Decorate means to make something look bright and special, so marigolds are flowers that people use to make a place look lovely.
explain: Some words have more than one kind. The dictionary says there are pot marigolds, and French or African marigolds. Pot marigolds are also called calendula. When a word has another name after "also called", or a list of kinds after "such as", you have found a clue that tells you more.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence. Try "Families decorate graves with bright orange flowers and make sugar skulls." It still makes sense, so orange flowers is a good meaning for marigolds in this sentence.
fact: A marigold is a garden plant with bright orange or yellow flowers.
fact: There are different kinds of marigold, such as pot marigolds (also called calendula) and French or African marigolds.
fact: Gardeners plant marigolds to help keep pests away.
fact: In India, marigold garlands are used at festivals like Diwali and at weddings.
fact: In Mexico, marigolds are used to decorate the Day of the Dead.
exercise: «Families decorate graves with orange marigolds.» What colour are the marigolds in this sentence? | *Orange | Blue | White | Purple
exercise: A gardener plants marigolds in her garden. Why might she do this? | To make the soil turn into rock | To cook them for dinner | To make the garden dark | *To help keep pests away
exercise: Pot marigolds are also called what? | Tulips | Daisies | Roses | *Calendula
test: «In India, marigold garlands are used at weddings.» Where are marigold garlands used? | On a football pitch | *At weddings | In a dentist's chair | At the seaside
test: Which of these is a kind of marigold? | Tulip | Sunflower | Rose | *French marigold
exam: What is a marigold? | A tall tree that grows in the forest | A kind of bread from Mexico | *A garden plant with bright orange or yellow flowers | A small insect that eats leaves
